INTRO = [
"Abdominal obesity marks visceral fat accumulation, and in Korean adults aged 30-90 years waist circumference has been associated with mortality independently of body mass index [@cho2018differential]. Korean guidelines define abdominal obesity as a waist circumference of at least 90 cm in men and 85 cm in women [@kim2021guidelines], and its prevalence has risen over the past 15 years, mainly among men [@kim2026obesity; @jeong2026nationwide].",
"Obesity is unevenly distributed across places as well as people. In Korea, abdominal obesity has been more common among women with less education and lower income [@yoo2010general; @jang2021trends], and small-area studies elsewhere have mapped wide local variation in obesity [@quick2020trends]. Area-level socioeconomic disadvantage is consistently associated with obesity [@area2023inequalities], while the evidence for specific obesogenic features of places, such as the food environment and walkability, is more mixed [@food2024environment; @walkability2019adults].",
"Most district-level obesity data in Korea come from self-reported height and weight in the Community Health Survey [@kang2015korea], which tend to underestimate body mass index [@maukonen2018comparison]. The national general health screening, which the National Health Insurance Service offers to insured adults [@cheolseong2017data], measures waist circumference in every attendee and publishes the number of attendees above the abdominal obesity cut-off by district and sex every year [@web:kosis2026metabolic]. These data describe measured central adiposity among the people who attend screening.",
"To the author's knowledge, no study has used these screening measurements to map abdominal obesity across all Korean districts or to ask which district characteristics follow it. This study described where measured abdominal obesity among screening attendees is more common than expected after standardization for sex and age, and examined its association with the food and mobility environment, risk behaviors and stress, and socioeconomic position, with attention to the reach of screening itself.",
]

IRB_FULL = "The Institutional Review Board of Hongik University approved the study on November 4, 2025 (7002340-202511-HR-012) and its continuing review on November 3, 2026 (7002340-202611-HR-040), and waived informed consent because only published aggregate statistics were used."
IRB_ANON = "The study was approved by an institutional review board, which waived informed consent because only published aggregate statistics were used (details on the title page). Reporting follows the STROBE statement, adapted for an ecological design (checklist provided as a separate file)."
def methods(N, th):
    return [
("Study design and data",
 f"This ecological panel study covered all {N['n_districts']} districts (si, gun, and gu) of the Republic of Korea from 2019 to 2024 ({th(N['n_rows'])} district-years). The outcome was the annual number of general health screening attendees whose measured waist circumference was at least 90 cm in men or 85 cm in women, the abdominal obesity component of the metabolic syndrome risk factors published by the National Health Insurance Service by district and sex [@kim2021guidelines; @web:kosis2026metabolic]. The denominator was the number of attendees in the same table, so the outcome describes prevalence conditional on attending screening, not prevalence in the whole resident population.",
 f"The table was checked against its components before modeling. From 2019 its attendee total closely matched the national number of general screening attendees (province-level ratios 0.98-1.00), whereas in 2018 it covered only about one third of attendees ({N['exam_full']['2018']:.1f} million of the 15.1 million attendees), the subset who also had lipid tests that year, a share that differed between provinces (0.31-0.36), and the national share with abdominal obesity rose to {N['rate_full']['2018']:.1f}% before returning to {N['rate_full']['2019']:.1f}% in 2019 (Supplementary Table S1). For 2013-2017 the table covered 5%-8% more people than the general screening count, uniformly across provinces. The waist cut-offs did not change. The principal analysis therefore used 2019-2024; 2013-2017 was analyzed separately and 2018 was excluded. Sejong, published only as a province row, and 1 district-year missing from the analysis copy were filled from the source tables, giving a complete panel.",
 "Expected counts were obtained by indirect standardization [@inskip1983methods]. National rates of abdominal obesity among attendees in 2 sexes and 15 age groups (19 years or younger, 13 five-year groups from 20-24 to 80-84 years, and 85 years or older) were applied to the attendee age structure of each district, approximated from the resident population by sex and age [@web:mois2026population] and national age-specific attendance and rescaled to the observed number of attendees of each sex. Expected counts were rescaled each year so that national expected and observed totals matched, so the ratios compare each district with the national level of the same year. Sex was taken as recorded in the screening statistics."),
("District characteristics",
 "The model used 10 characteristics in 4 groups (Supplementary Table S2). The food and mobility environment was represented by general restaurants and instant food businesses per 10,000 residents [@web:mois2026licence; @food2024environment], registered cars per capita, and the age-standardized walking rate from the Community Health Survey [@kang2015korea; @walkability2019adults]. Risk behaviors and stress were represented by the survey's high-risk drinking, current smoking, and perceived stress rates [@traversy2015alcohol; @morris2015heavier; @wardle2011stress]. Socioeconomic position was represented by the share of adults with tertiary education and the share of residents receiving basic livelihood security [@area2023inequalities; @jang2021trends]. Screening uptake, attendees as a share of those eligible, was included because wider attendance can bring in people with less adiposity. Self-reported obesity from the survey, a related but distinct adiposity measure based on body mass index, was examined only in a sensitivity model. All models included 5 fixed adjustments: urban population share, physicians per 1,000 residents, sex ratio, fiscal autonomy, and the share aged 80 years or older. Registered cars for Sejong were imputed by the yearly mean, and basic livelihood security rates for 2021-2023 with implausible values were set to missing and interpolated within districts (Supplementary Table S2). Characteristics were standardized to 1 SD."),
("Statistical analysis",
 "Counts were modeled with a negative binomial likelihood, chosen over the Poisson by the widely applicable information criterion (WAIC) in models with the fixed adjustments only [@gelman2014understanding], with the log of expected counts as the offset, a Besag-York-Mollié 2 district effect on a contact graph of 593 neighboring pairs [@besag1991bayesian; @riebler2016intuitive], and first-order random-walk and independent year effects, using penalized complexity priors [@simpson2017penalising] and integrated nested Laplace approximation [@rue2009approximate] in R [@web:rcore2026] with a single thread and fixed seeds; the principal model was fitted twice to confirm reproducibility. Results are rate ratios (RRs) per 1 SD with 95% credible intervals (CrIs). Spatial autocorrelation of district-mean residuals was tested with 2-sided Moran's I permutation tests (999 permutations), reported with the expected value under no autocorrelation; hot and cold spots were identified with the Getis-Ord Gi* statistic [@ord1995local].",
 "Robustness was assessed in 5 ways. First, 200 models used random subsets of the 10 characteristics with the 5 adjustments [@steegen2016increasing]. Second, Knorr-Held space-time interaction types I-IV were added [@knorrheld2000bayesian]. Third, Spatial+ and restricted spatial regression [@dupont2022spatial; @hodges2010adding], province-by-year random effects, characteristics lagged by 1 and 2 years, alternative district effects, the 2019-2021 and 2022-2024 windows, 2020-2024 only, the exclusion of 2020-2021, and region-specific slopes were fitted, and every specification listed in the Supplementary material is reported regardless of direction. Fourth, between-district means and within-district deviations of the characteristics credible in the principal model were separated [@bell2015explaining], and 3 negative-control exposures (hit-and-run accidents, the traffic culture index, and fires) were fitted [@lipsitch2010negative]. Fifth, models with the alternative contact graph, without the age-80 adjustment, with unstandardized expected counts, with self-reported obesity added, for 2013-2017, for 2013-2024 including 2018, and for metabolic syndrome from the same screening (228 districts; Sejong not available) as a comparison outcome were fitted.",
 IRB_ANON),
]
